<title>POLAND: Polish zloty fixed weaker at 2.90 pct from parity.</title>
<headline>Polish zloty fixed weaker at 2.90 pct from parity.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.0335 to the dollar, down from Wednesday's 3.0235 and at 1.8025 to the mark, also down from 1.7965, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.90 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Wednesday's 3.12 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
